# --- Local rollback snapshots stay out of git (ruling 2026-08-07) ---
# Snapshots are local rollback floors, not repo history. The repo holds the real
# version; backups stay on disk. Mirrors the rule in the 01-HPV repo.
*.pre_*
*.pre-*
*-pre[0-9]*
*.SUPERSEDED*

# --- Cruft ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# NOT ignored, deliberately: log-decision/log_decision_PATCHED.py
# It is a 2026-07-23 fork of the substrate writer, 96 lines divergent, whose
# ALLOWED_LANES is the stale two-lane set. It should be deleted, not silenced —
# and an ignore rule would hide it rather than resolve it. Leaving it untracked
# keeps it visible as `??` until Bill rules on it. See D24.
